      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for updating the message. It looks like the end of this paragraph still describes the `binder_alloc.c` changes that left the patch, though: the C allocator isn\u0027t touched any more, and the partial final page comes from aosp/4367601. Could you drop those two sentences? In the first paragraph, \"physical slice offset\" could also just be \"slice offset\", since `vm_slice_off` comes from the `mmap()` offset.\n\nIt would also help to say what fails without the patch, for example:\n\n```\nBinder inserts and zaps its pages one kernel page at a time. In a 4KB\nprocess, a mapping that starts inside a 16KB page makes the C allocator\nround buffer addresses below vm_start, so their pages[] index wraps. An\nmmap() offset that isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned sets vm_slice_off, so\nvm_insert_page() maps each page from below its address, and zapping the\n16KB at that address before the page is freed leaves part of it mapped.\n```",
      "isAi": true,
